.TH DANBY-HEARTBEAT 1
.SH NAME
danby-heartbeat \- Zeeman fast-slow heartbeat oscillator
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/heartbeat
.SH MODEL
epsilon x'=-(x^3-Tx+y);
y'=x-x0.
.PP
x is a fast muscle state, y a slow electrochemical drive, T tension, and x0
pacemaker bias.  The cubic fast nullcline and slow feedback produce relaxation
oscillations.  The equilibrium is x=x0, y=Tx0-x0^3.
.SH DISPLAY
The left phase portrait plots drive against muscle state and reveals the fast
jumps and slow recovery branches.  The right plot shows both signed states
against time.  A nonnegative compartment plot would incorrectly clip half of
the cycle and is therefore not used.
.SH CONTROLS
Drag the phase portrait to set both states.  Tracks set epsilon, tension, and
pacemaker bias.  Space pauses, period steps, r resets, and q exits.
.SH NUMERICS
The analytic equilibrium is checked by
.B temple/danbytest.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/danby/heartbeat.b
.br
.B /appl/temple/heartbeat.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR numerics (2),
.IR plot (2)
